{"raw": {"https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#admissions-counselor": {"title": "Admissions Counselor", "description": "Admissions Counselor. The Admissions Counselor's responsibilities include recruiting extensively and traveling (a minimum of 12 weeks) and managing a geographic territory; conducting oral presentations about Mercyhurst to a variety of constituents, including prospective students and parents, school counselors, and college personnel; reviewing applications and scholarship considerations; developing and maintaining individual recruitment files/records; telemarketing and social media initiatives with prospective students; assisting prospective students with admission and financial aid; awarding financial aid to prospective students; participating in on-campus and regional college events; working weeknights and weekends as needed; and managing admission initiatives independently. Learn more about this opportunity via the Admissions Counselor position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#aim-student-support-coordinator": {"title": "AIM Student Support Coordinator", "description": "AIM Student Support Coordinator. The AIM Student Support Coordinator supports neurodivergent students as they navigate college and their careers, has direct involvement with neurodivergent students, their family, faculty, staff, and agencies that support their participation in AIM; and provides direct academic and other support for students in the program. Responsibilities include administrative, direct services, program development, and public relations/outreach. Learn more about this opportunity via the AIM Student Support Coordinator position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#bus-driver-part-time": {"title": "Bus Driver (Part Time)", "description": "Bus Driver (Part Time). Bus Drivers safely operate a passenger bus or van that transports athletes and other approved persons to and from athletic events or other designated locations while adhering promptly to time schedules. Responsible for the preparation of records and basic reports on routine maintenance, mechanical malfunction, accidents, and/or incidents with buses and/or equipment. Part-time position. Learn more about this opportunity via the Bus Driver position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#clinical-operations-coordinator": {"title": "Clinical Operations Coordinator", "description": "Clinical Operations Coordinator. The Clinical Operations Coordinator coordinates, implements, and continuously improves operational processes supporting the clinical phase of the program; manages day-to-day logistics of clinical education, including student placements, preceptor onboarding, processing of affiliation agreements, and compliance tracking; supports the director of clinical education, who retains full responsibility for clinical education policies, student evaluation, curriculum development, site approval, and accreditation compliance. Responsibilities include reporting and authority structure, clinical operations and logistics, clinical site and preceptor coordination, accreditation and ongoing program assessment, operational support and process improvement, as well as communication and coordination. Learn more about this opportunity via the Clinical Operations Coordinator position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#director-of-sponsored-programs-and-grants": {"title": "Director of Sponsored Programs and Grants", "description": "Director of Sponsored Programs and Grants. The Director of Sponsored Programs and Grants identifies prospects for foundation and government grants that align with strategic projects, research, and programs developed by faculty and administration of the university; mediates and/or advocates for Mercyhurst University interests and builds relations with other organizations and entities whose interests are similar or whose functions affect Mercyhurst University; as well as develops and maintains effective strategies for solicitation and manages all follow-up and grant reporting activities. Responsibilities include reporting to the vice president for academic affairs and is responsible for the Department of Sponsored Programs and Grants (the position will have one direct report: the grant administrator); overseeing all academic and administrative departments in planning, organizing, and authoring grant and contract proposals and coordinating reporting and other post-award requirements; preparing a monthly report of grant activity and grants that have been awarded to the VP for academic affairs (an annual report is also prepared that summarizes the grant activity for the year and the outcomes of that activity); utilizing contacts to identify grant funding opportunities and research and developing grant applications for Mercyhurst University; identifying public and private funding sources that align with the university's strategic plan and work with appropriate departments in pursuing grant and contract opportunities; working with university leadership to implement new program initiatives that will foster positive community relations and support long term strategic goals; identifying, cultivating, and soliciting a portfolio of current and future donors from corporations, foundations, and government agencies; writing compelling letters, appeals, and proposals and preparing dynamic presentations customized for target audience; managing a professional presence at alumni and fundraising events, to raise awareness of Mercyhurst; and engaging major donors that will share the passion of the Mercyhurst mission, vision, and core values. Learn more about this opportunity via the Director of Sponsored Programs and Grants position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-admissions-assistant": {"title": "PT Admissions Assistant", "description": "PT Admissions Assistant. The PT Admissions Assistant responsibilities include reporting to the department chair/program director of the Department of Physician Assistant Studies and will work closely with the admissions chair as well as all faculty involved in the admissions process; assisting/serving on the admissions committee in the recruitment and selection of applicants and/or ongoing analysis of the admission process and candidate pool; vetting approximately 150-200 applicants throughout the admissions cycle; performing professional review and evaluation of candidate applications; completing applicant review sheets and updating Excel tracking forms in a timely manner; participating in both Zoom and in person interviews throughout the admissions cycle; coordinating with the admissions chair to schedule interviews, reviewing and maintaining the wait list, and calling accepted candidates; and attending the annual admissions meeting following completion of an admissions cycle. Learn more about this opportunity via the PT Admissions Assistant position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-counselor": {"title": "PT Counselor", "description": "PT Counselor. The PT Counselor provides screenings, counseling, psychoeducation, crisis intervention, and related services to Mercyhurst University students through the Counseling Center and consults with faculty and staff on the campus as indicated to assist in outreach and intervention for students. Responsibilities include providing initial screening and assessment of student to determine clinical needs, acuity, and treatment plan; establishing effective rapport with most students offering courtesy, compassion, and hospitality; providing brief and ongoing therapy using individual, group, couples, family, or crisis modalities; utilizing a variety of therapy approaches in a knowledgeable and competent manner based on the individual needs of each student in a manner consistent with clinical best practice and professional standards; staffing the urgent walk-in hours at the center and assisting with student crisis situations that arise during the workday; conducting safety assessments on students and working collaboratively with university departments and community resources to effectively coordinate rapid and effective responses when safety is an issue; maintaining appropriate professional records on each client and communicating client information in a confidential and professional manner consistent with Pennsylvania law and professional organization codes of ethics (ex. APA); providing consultation services to faculty, staff, parents/family, and students to enhance personal development and wellness; assuring that all office procedures, policies, and required reports are developed, followed, and completed in a timely fashion; working with the executive director for the development and implementation of treatment planning and behavioral goals; informing the executive director of any difficulties relating to treatment issues, concerns around student safety, procedural, patient satisfaction, and other departmental or public relations concerns; and working with the executive director to develop and implement annual goals and objectives for the Counseling Center and wellness initiatives. Learn more about this opportunity via the PT Counselor position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-registered-nurse": {"title": "PT Registered Nurse", "description": "PT Registered Nurse. The PT Registered Nurse provides primary health care to the university students within the accepted professional nursing standards and protocols approved by the Pennsylvania State Board of Nursing. Responsibilities include developing and carrying out individualized care plans that support the physical, emotional, psychological, and social well-being of students; working collaboratively with physicians and the clinical team to ensure high-quality, coordinated care; performing physical assessments, making nursing diagnoses, and providing treatment (including prescriptive medicine under standing orders); educating students about their health conditions, treatment options, and preventive measures to promote lifelong wellness; identifying current and potential health risks, guiding students toward healthier choices and safer behaviors; maintaining accurate, clear, and timely documentation of visits, assessments, and treatment plans; communicating important clinical, safety, and student health concerns to leadership in a proactive, solutions-focused way; providing appropriate health information to parents when authorized by student consent; welcoming every student with compassion, courtesy, and respect, upholding a strong \u201cstudent-first\u201d philosophy and honoring diversity and inclusion; leading and supporting campus-wide health initiatives, including flu vaccine clinics, TB testing, health form reviews, and student physicals; serving as a key partner with faculty in the Physician Assistant program; acting as a trusted health resource and educator for the entire campus community; helping develop policies, protocols, and quality assurance programs that strengthen clinical care; pursuing ongoing professional growth through continuing education and licensure requirements; and supporting the overall operations of the Health Center, including supply management and other essential tasks. Learn more about this opportunity via the PT Registered Nurse position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#adjunct-faculty-student-success-coordinator": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Student Success Coordinator", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Student Success Coordinator. The Adjunct Faculty - Student Success Coordinator provides centralized coordination of the Physician Assistant Program's Student Success Process and academic support for students throughout the program. Responsibilities include reviewing Preliminary Self-Assessment information submitted by students in preparation for Student Success Meeting; conducting required Self-Assessment and Performance Reflection (SAP) meetings with students; assisting students in identifying factors contributing to academic performance; working with students to develop individualized strategies for improvement; providing academic coaching and support; providing referrals to faculty or university resources when additional assistance is indicated; completing and maintaining Student Success documentation; monitoring student progress and providing follow-up academic support; collaborating with faculty advisors, course directors, and the Student Success Committee. Learn more about this opportunity via the Adjunct Faculty - Student Success Coordinator position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#adjunct-instructor": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Adjunct Instructor. The Adjunct Instructor teaches psychology in healthcare, clinical skills labs, procedures in medicine lab, and/or pediatrics, as well as supports the Mercy mission and the Department of Physician Assistant Studies\u2019 mission, vision, and goals. Responsibilities include teaching a section of a course or a specific unit within a course; engaging in student assessment/evaluation activities, as well as providing students with feedback and support throughout the course; and teaching multiple courses offered in the graduate Physician Assistant Studies program. Learn more about this opportunity via the Adjunct Instructor position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#assistant-professor-of-physician-assistant-studies": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies", "description": "Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies. The Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies works closely with senior faculty to ensure the program meets and exceeds the accreditation standards set forth by the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA); prepares physician assistant students to be leaders in the profession, proficient in meeting the challenges of healthcare, and provide compassionate, quality care to the diverse communities in which they serve; provides the opportunity to be involved in both the didactic and clinical phases of the program and can be adjusted to the applicant\u2019s interest and area of expertise; and participates in ongoing program assessment and evaluation, student advising, and departmental committee work. Responsibilities include working with the director of didactic education in the development and implementation of curriculum; providing instruction during the didactic year within areas of expertise and training; developing, implementing, and assessing academic performance evaluations within the didactic phase; participating in academic advising of students; as well as participating in ongoing evaluation and self-evaluation to demonstrate effectiveness in areas of teaching, scholarship, and service. Learn more about this opportunity via the Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#education-adjunct-instructor": {"title": "Education Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Education Adjunct Instructor. The Education Adjunct Instructor teaches collaboratively with program faculty in undergraduate and/or graduate education courses; supports courses in areas such as early childhood education, special education, inclusive practices, assessment, classroom management, literacy, educational psychology, instructional methods, field-based experiences, and related areas; and supports the Mercyhurst University mission and the Department of Education\u2019s commitment to preparing reflective, ethical, and effective educators who are responsive to the needs of diverse learners. Responsibilities include teaching a full course section and supervising course-related field-based experiences; preparing and delivering course content, facilitating student engagement, assessing student learning, providing timely feedback, supporting students\u2019 professional development, and maintaining communication with department faculty; and teaching in one or more undergraduate or graduate courses offered through the Department of Education, depending on qualifications, experience, and departmental need. Learn more about this opportunity via the Education Adjunct Instructor position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#instructor-of-nursing": {"title": "Instructor of Nursing", "description": "Instructor of Nursing. The Instructor of Nursing conducts classroom and clinical laboratory instruction designed to teach nursing students theoretical and clinical aspects of promotion, maintenance, and restoration of health to clients across the life span; researches, prepares, and presents lectures, assigns outside studies, and regularly assesses the student\u2019s progress; develops, assigns, and evaluates clinical activities to assure practical application of nursing theory; as well as participates in curriculum development and fosters the mission of Mercyhurst University and the philosophy and goals of the Nursing program. Responsibilities include abiding by the Faculty Duties and Responsibilities listed in the Mercyhurst University Faculty Handbook, Section IV; preparing course outlines and curriculum content in assigned subject area, in concert with the chair and program director(s); conducting appropriate research to ensure that course content and lectures incorporate current trends, techniques, and developments in nursing practice; demonstrating expertise in classroom presentations of theory and clinical laboratory activities; guiding, structuring, and evaluating student performance in theory and clinical; maintaining clinical expertise by attending at least one workshop related to area of expertise each year; maintaining currency in CPR; meeting regularly with students to review their progress; developing strategies that increase the retention of qualified students within the program; maintaining files and records on student classroom and clinical performance; submitting grades to the director and, according to policy, to the Registrar; maintaining positive communication with various departments within the university, affiliating agencies, and community by participating in committees and through volunteer work; and meeting weekly with teaching team to discuss the course progression, plan and coordinate clinical activities, and discuss student progression. Learn more about this opportunity via the Instructor of Nursing position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#part-time-assistant-professor-of-physician-assistant-studies": {"title": "Part-Time Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies", "description": "Part-Time Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies. The Part-Time Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies works with the director of didactic education in the development and implementation of curriculum; provides instruction during the didactic year within areas of expertise and training; develops, implements, and assesses academic performance evaluations within the didactic phase; supports the Admissions Committee by working with the director of admissions on various responsibilities throughout the calendar year; assists the program with on-going accreditation work to meet the accreditation standards set for by the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA); and participates in the Program Development Committee and Curriculum Committee meetings. Learn more about this opportunity via the Part-Time Assistant Professor of Physician Assistant Studies position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#assistant-women-s-lacrosse-coach": {"title": "Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach", "description": "Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach. The Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach responsibilities include recruiting, training, and coaching members of the Lacrosse program; promoting academic excellence, integrity, and graduation; monitoring academic progress, academic meetings, class scheduling, and attendance; coordinating team travel for competitions to include van or bus itineraries, lodging, and meals; planning, promoting, and conducting camps, clinics, and/or lessons; assisting in fundraising efforts; developing meaningful relationships with prospective, current, and former student-athletes; representing Mercyhurst University and the Lacrosse program in a professional manner; and performing other related duties incidental to the work described herein. Learn more about this opportunity via the Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#athletic-trainer": {"title": "Athletic Trainer", "description": "Athletic Trainer. The Athletic Trainer works under the supervision of the director of athletic training services and supervises the care of student-athletes participating in Mercyhurst University\u2019s Athletic program. Responsibilities include preventing, evaluating, managing, and rehabilitating injuries within the university\u2019s comprehensive Sports Medicine program. Learn more about this opportunity via the Athletic Trainer position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#autism-support-initiative-special-education-instructional-technician-graduate-assistant": {"title": "Autism Support Initiative \u2013 Special Education Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant", "description": "Autism Support Initiative \u2013 Special Education Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant. The Autism Support Initiative \u2013 Special Education Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant collaborates with the graduate assistant Special Education teacher and other graduate assistant instructional technicians in the provision of evidence-based special education services contracted with a Local Educational Agency (LEA). Responsibilities include providing skill instruction to all students and assisting with curricular programming/development; collecting, graphing, and analyzing student behavioral and academic data; assisting with meeting children\u2019s personal and healthcare needs, as necessary; and assisting the Special Education teacher with materials preparation and the ongoing operation of the classroom. Learn more about this opportunity via the Autism Support Initiative \u2013 Special Education Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#graduate-assistant-for-athletic-communications": {"title": "Graduate Assistant for Athletic Communications", "description": "Graduate Assistant for Athletic Communications. The Graduate Assistant for Athletic Communications contributes to the Athletics Department website and all social media platforms, with content type ranging from written, graphic design, and multimedia/video; compiles, disseminates, and maintains sports statistics for assigned teams, including serving as official scorekeeper for home games; directly manages setup, live production, and breakdown of webcast equipment; manages student employees and game-day event staff for all home games for assigned sports in a professional setting; plans and implements historical statistic archiving, as well as maintenance of photography database; completes conference, regional, and national award applications to recognize coaches and student-athletes from assigned teams and programs; and travels with teams as necessary, primarily for postseason contests. Learn more about this opportunity via the Graduate Assistant for Athletic Communications position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#graduate-assistant-for-men-s-lacrosse": {"title": "Graduate Assistant for Men's Lacrosse", "description": "Graduate Assistant for Men's Lacrosse. Responsibilities for the Graduate Assistant for Men's Lacrosse includes recruiting, training, and coaching members of the Lacrosse program; promoting academic excellence, integrity, and graduation; monitoring academic progress, academic meetings, class scheduling, and attendance; coordinating team travel for competitions to include van or bus itineraries, lodging, and meals; planning, promoting, and conducting camps, clinics, and/or lessons; assisting in fundraising efforts; developing meaningful relationships with prospective, current, and former student-athletes; and representing Mercyhurst University and the Lacrosse program in a professional manner. Learn more about this opportunity via the Graduate Assistant for Men's Lacrosse position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#graduate-assistant-for-women-s-lacrosse": {"title": "Graduate Assistant for Women's Lacrosse", "description": "Graduate Assistant for Women's Lacrosse. The Graduate Assistant for Women's Lacrosse responsibilities include recruiting, training, and coaching members of the Lacrosse program; promoting academic excellence, integrity, and graduation; monitoring academic progress, academic meetings, class scheduling, and attendance; coordinating team travel for competitions to include van or bus itineraries, lodging, and meals; planning, promoting, and conducting camps, clinics, and/or lessons; assisting in fundraising efforts; developing meaningful relationships with prospective, current, and former student-athletes; and representing Mercyhurst University and the Lacrosse program in a professional manner. Learn more about this opportunity via the Graduate Assistant for Women's Lacrosse position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#multi-tiered-systems-of-support-instructional-technician-graduate-assistant": {"title": "Multi-Tiered Systems of Support \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant", "description": "Multi-Tiered Systems of Support \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant. The Multi-Tiered Systems of Support \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant collaborates with other graduate assistant MTSS instructional technicians, district MTSS faculty/staff, and the program director/clinical supervisor in the provision of evidence-based educational services contracted with a Local Educational Agency (LEA). Responsibilities include providing instruction to identified students and assisting with curricular programming/development in small group and 1:1 settings; collecting, graphing, and analyzing student academic/functional performance data; assisting the district MTSS faculty/staff with materials preparation; and attending MTSS meetings, assigned trainings, and collaborates with MTSS faculty/staff. Learn more about this opportunity via the Multi-Tiered Systems of Support \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant position summary. Learn More"}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#preschool-instructional-technician-graduate-assistant": {"title": "Preschool \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant", "description": "Preschool \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant. The Preschool \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant collaborates with the preschool director, classroom teachers and assistants, families, and the program director/clinical supervisor in the provision of evidence-based educational services contracted with a local preschool program. Responsibilities include providing instruction to identified students and assisting with curricular programming/development in large group, small group, and 1:1 settings; collecting, graphing, and analyzing student academic/functional performance data; completing materials preparation for student(s), as needed; attending assigned trainings; and collaborating with families, preschool teachers, and assistants. Learn more about this opportunity via the Preschool \u2013 Instructional Technician Graduate Assistant position summary. Learn More"}}, "rows": {"https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#admissions-counselor": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#admissions-counselor", "job_title_in_post": "Admissions Counselor", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#aim-student-support-coordinator": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#aim-student-support-coordinator", "job_title_in_post": "AIM Student Support Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#bus-driver-part-time": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#bus-driver-part-time", "job_title_in_post": "Bus Driver (Part Time)", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#clinical-operations-coordinator": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#clinical-operations-coordinator", "job_title_in_post": "Clinical Operations Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#director-of-sponsored-programs-and-grants": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#director-of-sponsored-programs-and-grants", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Sponsored Programs and Grants", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Sponsored Programs and Grants", "area_key_words": "Sponsored Programs and Grants", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-admissions-assistant": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-admissions-assistant", "job_title_in_post": "PT Admissions Assistant", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-counselor": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-counselor", "job_title_in_post": "PT Counselor", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-registered-nurse": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#pt-registered-nurse", "job_title_in_post": "PT Registered Nurse", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#adjunct-faculty-student-success-coordinator": {"school_id": 1152, "posting_url": "https://www.mercyhurst.edu/human-resources/jobs#adjunct-faculty-student-success-coordinator", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Faculty - Student Success Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "